\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For December 28\b0\par\par\uc2 1,311 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Dezember 2010\par 08:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par MACRO/\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 /FIXED INCOME: \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: RECOVERY IN PRODUCTION BRIGHTENS JAPAN OUTLOOK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's industrial output rose for the first time in six months in November and is expected to gain more in the near future, the government said Tuesday, soothing concerns that ongoing deflationary pressures will lead to a sharp economic slowdown. (published 0604 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  THREATENS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  AS YEN HITS 3-WEEK HIGH \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister Tuesday described the yen's recent rises as "one-sided" and threatened to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  again in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to curb its strength, as the yen marked three-week highs against the dollar--a cause for nervousness among Japanese exporters. (published 0504 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA SAFE: 3RD-QUARTER CURRENT ACCOUNT SURPLUS $102.3 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's third-quarter current account surplus totaled $102.3 billion, data released by China's State Administration of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  showed Tuesday. (published 0354 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par THAI FINANCE MINISTRY REVISES UP 2010 GDP GROWTH FORECAST TO 7.8% FROM 7.5% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Tuesday revised up its 2010 economic growth forecast to 7.8%, from 7.5% projected three months earlier, citing robust economic momentum in the first nine months and continuous strong performance in the export sector. (published 0628 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INDONESIA FINANCE MINISTER: 2010 BUDGET DEFICIT LIKELY ONLY 1.1% OF GDP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Indonesian government will likely run a budget deficit equal to 1.1% of gross domestic product this year, Finance Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Agus Martowardojo\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Tuesday. (published 0631 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par THAI NOV MANUFACTURING PRODUCTION INDEX +5.6% ON YEAR - MINISTRY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's Manufacturing Production Index, or MPI, rose 5.6% from a year earlier to 190.36 in November, according to preliminary data from the Ministry of Industry's Office of Industrial Economics. (published 0614 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: INDIA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  PAYMENTS DIRECTIVE TO HIT IRAN TRADE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Monday imposed what is effectively a curb on trade with Iran, in an indication of New Delhi's growing closeness with Washington. (published 0551 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =PREVIEW: TAIWAN LIKELY TO HIKE INTEREST RATES THURSDAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Despite moderate inflation, Taiwan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will likely raise interest rates for the third time this year at its quarterly meeting Thursday, as it seeks to normalize lending costs from previously ultra-low levels and to cool the sizzling property market. (published 0624 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par EQUITIES: \par  \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 LG GROUP\f28 \uc2 \f2  TARGETS RECORD ANNUAL SALES OF KRW156 TLN IN 2011, UP 11% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's \f28 \uc2 \f2 LG Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  Tuesday said it is targeting record annual sales of KRW156 trillion in 2011, an 11% increase from this year's level of around KnRW141 trillion. (published 0218 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: DAI-ICHI LIFE TO BUY TOWER AUSTRALIA GROUP FOR ABOUT Y100B \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dai-ichi Life Insurance Co. will make \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tower Australia Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . a wholly owned unit for about Y100 billion, a person familiar with the matter told Dow Jones Newswires on Tuesday. (published 0430 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: CHINATRUST MADE HIGHEST BID FOR NAN SHAN - TAIWAN LEGISLATOR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinatrust Financial Holding Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . submitted the highest bid out of the four companies interested in buying \f28 \uc2 \f2 American International Group Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s Taiwan life insurance unit, a Taiwan legislator said Tuesday. (published 0512 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par TOSHIBA: BOUGHT STAKE IN HARD-DISK DRIVE R&D JV FROM FUJITSU \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Toshiba Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has bought a stake in a hard disk drive research and development joint venture from its partner \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fujitsu Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . to make the unit 100%-owned, the two companies said in a joint press release Tuesday. (published 0226 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: PATNI COMPUTER FOUNDING FAMILY STILL DIFFERS OVER SALE - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Differences persist among the founders of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Patni Computer Systems Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . over a deal to sell their and private equity firm General Atlantic's combined 63% stake in the company, a person familiar with the matter said Tuesday. (published 0644 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: CHINA CONSTRUCTION BANK, CHINA LIFE BUY STAKE IN ING VENTURE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Construction Bank Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has moved closer to controlling an insurance joint venture being sold by \f28 \uc2 \f2 ING Groep NV\f28 \uc2 \f2  and its former Chinese partner, after a consortium led by CCB and Taiwan's China Life Insurance Co. bought the remaining 50% stake that had been put up for sale for CNY950 million . (published 0359 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par KUNLUN ENERGY TO BUY FROM PETROCHINA FOR CNY18.9 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Kunlun Energy Co. will buy a natural gas transmission company from its parent \f28 \uc2 \f2 PetroChina Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . for CNY18.9 billion, the companies said in a joint statement Monday. (published 0024 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PICC PROPERTY & CASUALTY: PREMIUM INCOME FOR JAN 1-DEC 24 PERIOD CNY150 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PICC Property & Casualty Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., China's largest non-life insurer by premiums, said Monday its direct premium income between Jan. 1 and Dec. 24 totaled CNY150 billion. (published 2351 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: PTT TARGETS ANNUAL REVENUE GROWTH OF 10% OVER NEXT 5 YEARS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PTT PCL\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Thailand's largest energy conglomerate by revenue, expects its revenue to grow 10% annually over the next five years, likely reaching THB3 trillion by 2015, Chief Financial Officer Tevin Vongvanich said. (published 0302 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BANK MANDIRI TO ISSUE 2.34 BLN RIGHTS SHARES IN JANUARY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PT \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Mandiri\f28 \uc2 \f2  said in a prospectus Tuesday that it plans to issue 2.34 billion rights shares on Jan. 27 at an offering price of IDR4,000 to IDR6,150 for each unit. (published 0140 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SK ENERGY, FORMOSA SIGN PACT TO JOINTLY DEVELOP RECHARGEABLE BATTERIES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's \f28 \uc2 \f2 SK Energy Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday it has signed a memorandum of understanding with Taiwan's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Formosa Plastics Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . to jointly develop rechargeable batteries used in energy storage systems. (published 0640 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE:ASIAN SHARES MIXED; FINANCIALS WEAK IN SHANGHAI \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian stock markets were mixed Tuesday with the Japanese market weighed by profit-taking while securities firms fell in China as investors fretted over the possibility of further monetary tightening measures from Beijing. (published 0350 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par ENERGY/COMMODITIES: \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: CHINA STARTS ANTI-DUMPING PROBE INTO US DISTILLER'S DRIED GRAINS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's Ministry of Commerce said Tuesday it has opened an anti-dumping investigation into U.S. exports of distiller's dried grains, a livestock feed that the U.S. farm industry lobby has sought to promote among Chinese feed mills. (published 0455 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par VIETNAM, RUSSIA SIGN PACT TO EXTEND OIL COOPERATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vietnam and Russia have signed an agreement to continue oil exploration and production cooperation in Vietnamese waters by extending the life of an oil joint venture beyond 2010, the Vietnamese government said Tuesday. (published 0339 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SK ENERGY PLANS TO SELL NEW NAPHTHA CRACKING TECHNOLOGY OVERSEAS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean oil refiner \f28 \uc2 \f2 SK Energy Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . plans in cooperation with U.S.-based \f28 \uc2 \f2 KBR Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . to sell proprietary naphtha cracking technology in overseas markets including China, a spokesman for the Korean company said Tuesday. (published 0255 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA FORMER OFFICIAL: GLOBAL RARE EARTH DEMAND TO REACH 250,000 TONS BY 2015 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Global rare earth demand will keep rising "for a long time," and could reach 250,000 metric tons in five years, the retired head of a key department of China's Ministry of Industry & Information Technology said Tuesday. (published 0154 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BMD CPO FUTURES HIT FRESH 33-MONTH HIGH; ARGENTINA CROP CONCERNS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crude palm oil futures on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bursa Malaysia\f28 \uc2 \f2  Derivatives rose to a fresh 33-month high Tuesday, driven by concerns over dry weather in major soybean exporter Argentina, traders said. (published 0243 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INDONESIA OFFICIAL: MINING INVESTMENT COULD RISE 20% TO $2.3B 2011 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia expects investment in its mineral and coal sectors to rise by around 20% to $2.3 billion next year, a Department of Energy & Mineral Resources official said Tuesday. (published 0314 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par VIETNAM 2010-11 COFFEE OUTPUT LIKELY 1 MLN TONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vietnam's coffee output in the current crop year will likely be 1 million metric tons, or 16.67 million 60-kilogram bags, the Ministry of Industry and Trade said Tuesday. (published 0513 GMT) [ 28-12-10 0704GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020101228e6cs0009o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
