\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 435 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Dezember 2010\par 07:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: JAPAN INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT UP IN NOVEMBER; OUTLOOK POSITIVE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's industrial output rose for the first time in six months in November and is expected to gain more in the near future, the government said Tuesday, soothing concerns that ongoing deflationary pressures will lead to a sharp economic slowdown. (published 0256 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  THREATENS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  AS YEN HITS 3-WEEK HIGH \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister Tuesday described the yen's recent rises as "one-sided" and threatened to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  again in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to curb its strength, as the yen marked three-week highs against the dollar--a cause for nervousness among Japanese exporters. (published 0504 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA SAFE: 3RD-QUARTER CURRENT ACCOUNT SURPLUS $102.3 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's third-quarter current account surplus totaled $102.3 billion, data released by China's State Administration of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  showed Tuesday. (published 0354 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA FINANCE MINISTER: 2011 FISCAL DEFICIT TARGET LIKELY CNY900 BLN - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese Finance Minister Xie Xuren said the government will likely aim for a fiscal deficit of CNY900 billion in 2011, comprising a central government deficit of CNY700 billion and CNY200 billion in debt issued by the central government on behalf of local governments, the 21st Century Business Herald reported Tuesday. (published 0510 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA ECONOMIST BA: RATE HIKES POSSIBLE IN 1ST HALF - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could raise interest rates to alleviate negative real interest rates in the first half of next year while inflation pressures are large, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -backed Financial News reported Tuesday, citing Ba Shusong, an economist at a government think tank. (published 0101 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN NOVEMBER OVERALL RETAIL SALES +1.3% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese retail sales rose 1.3% in November from a year earlier, the Ministry of Economy, Trade and Industry said Tuesday, bouncing back from a 0.2% on-year fall in the previous month. (published 2359 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PBOC RAISES 1-YEAR BILL YIELD BY 17 BPS TO 2.5115% AFTER RATE HIKE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Thursday it sold CNY1 billion worth of one-year bills at 2.5115%, up nearly 17 basis points from the 2.3437% yield on the one-year bills it had issued in the past seven weeks, following its latest interest rate hike. (published 0235 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: INDIA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  PAYMENTS DIRECTIVE TO HIT IRAN TRADE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Monday imposed what is effectively a curb on trade with Iran, in an indication of New Delhi's growing closeness with Washington. (published 0551 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 28-12-10 0600GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020101228e6cs0007m\par }\page {\par\f