\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For November 8\b0\par\par\uc2 1,729 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 November 2010\par 08:11\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ: JAPAN ECONOMIC RECOVERY PAUSING; PACE OF GROWTH PACE TO SLOW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan said in its monthly economic report for November that the nation's economic recovery "seems to be pausing" although there are still "signs of a moderate recovery," using a slightly weaker tone than in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's previous report in October. (published 0519 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN FINANCE MINISTER NODA: STRONG YEN HAS ADVANTAGES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance minister emphasized Monday that the strong yen has "advantages," urging domestic companies to use it buy foreign firms and assets. (published 0054 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN INTERVENED\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MARKET ONLY ONCE IN SEPTEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Official data on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  showed Friday that the authorities waded into the market only once in the July-September period, lowering expectations there could be fresh attempts to drive the yen down, even as it remains near a record high against the dollar. (published 0411 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: GEITHNER SEEKS TO BOLSTER INDIA TIES AHEAD OF G-20 SUMMIT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Seeking to bolster strategic ties with India, U.S. Treasury Secretary Timothy Geithner Monday praised the emerging economy's balanced growth and exchange-rate flexibility. (published 0134 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA MINISTER: 2010 INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT TO RISE OVER 13.5% - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's industrial output will likely rise by more than 13.5% this year, and the country's chances of meeting its full-year energy efficiency targets have increased, the China Securities Journal reported Monday, citing Minister of Industry and Information Technology Li Yizhong. (published 0059 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S FINANCE MINISTER WARNS HIGHER A$ TO HURT REVENUES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's Finance Minister Penny Wong warned Monday the surging Australian dollar is eating into projections for government revenues, which will be reflected in its mid-year economic forecasts due for release Tuesday. (published 0657 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: S KOREA MAY TIGHTEN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  DERIVATIVES RULES PENDING PROBE OUTCOME \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean regulators may tighten existing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  derivatives regulations depending on the results of a scheduled probe into banks' activities in the market, a senior government official said Monday, as Seoul grows increasingly wary of the systemic threat posed by rapid foreign capital flows. (published 0422 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: NZ GOVERNMENT 3-MONTH OPERATING DEFICIT WIDER THAN FORECAST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The New Zealand government's core operating deficit was wider than forecast in the three months ended Sept. 30 due to the impact of the Canterbury earthquake and lower-than-forecast tax revenue, the Treasury said Monday. (published 0048 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BANK OF THAILAND\f28 \uc2 \f2 : NO SIGNS OF ECONOMIC BUBBLE FORMING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  hasn't detected any signs of economic bubbles forming, despite price increases in certain domestic assets, Senior Director Mathee Supapongse said Monday. (published 0647 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GOODMAN GROUP PRICES 10-YEAR US$325M BOND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goodman Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Monday it priced a US$325 million 10-year debt issue. (published 0340 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: EXIM BANK TO OFFER UP TO CNY5 BLN BONDS IN HK AT 2.65% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Export-Import Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Monday it plans to offer up to CNY5 billion worth of yuan-denominated bonds in Hong Kong from Tuesday to Nov. 26. (published 0535 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OCBC SEEKS TO RAISE $500 MLN VIA 12-YEAR LOWER TIER 2 ISSUE - SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Oversea-Chinese Banking Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is seeking to raise $500 million through a lower Tier-2 note issue, people familiar with the transaction said Monday. (published 0411 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =PREVIEW: JAPAN 3Q GDP GROWTH SEEN UP, BUT RISK OF RECESSION AHEAD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's economic expansion likely accelerated in the third quarter of 2010 as shoppers scrambled to buy cars before government subsidies ran out, air conditioners to stay cool in a scorching summer, and cigarettes before a new tobacco tax kicked in. (published 0425 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =PREVIEW: CHINA OCTOBER TRADE SURPLUS LIKELY REBOUNDED TO $26.4 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's trade surplus likely rebounded in October after narrowing in September, which would give critics of the country's exchange rate policy extra ammunition just as leaders of the Group of 20 industrial and developing nations gather in Seoul later this week to debate global imbalances. (published 0437 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SHELL TO SELL ABOUT A THIRD OF WOODSIDE STAKE FOR A$3.31B \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Royal Dutch Shell PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Monday that it has agreed to sell just under a third of its holding in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Woodside Petroleum Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . to equity investors for A$3.31 billion. (published 0626 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: SPHERE MINERALS: ACORN CAPITAL TO ACCEPT XTRATA'S OFFER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The second-largest shareholder in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sphere Minerals Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . will accept \f28 \uc2 \f2 Xstrata Plc\f28 \uc2 \f2 's A$513.6 million offer for the Mauritania-focused iron ore miner, giving a crucial advantage to the Anglo-Swiss miner in its battle for the company with a consortium of Chinese steelmakers. (published 0516 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ENTEKHAB: SIGNED FINAL CONTRACT TO ACQUIRE DAEWOO ELECTRONICS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Iranian home appliance maker Entekhab Industrial Group Monday said it has signed a final contract to acquire South Korea's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Daewoo Electronics Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . with the firm's creditors. (published 0445 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: ORICA FY PROFIT JUMPS TO A$1.3B AFTER DULUX DEMERGER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Explosives and chemicals company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Orica Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday that trading conditions have continued to improve this financial year and forecast annual profit to rise. (published 0047 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GOODBABY TO RAISE UP TO US$190 MLN IN HK IPO - TERM SHEET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Goodbaby International Holdings Ltd., China's largest maker of childcare products, plans to raise as much as US$190 million in an initial public offering in Hong Kong ahead of its listing on the Hong Kong stock exchange Nov. 24, according to a term sheet seen by Dow Jones Newswires on Monday. (published 0152 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA'S SOVEREIGN WEALTH FUND SETS UP HONG KONG UNIT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Investment Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., China's $300 billion sovereign-wealth fund, said Monday it has formed a wholly-owned unit in Hong Kong to expand its overseas investments. (published 2317 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA TAKEOVERS PANEL REJECTS LEIGHTON/HOCHTIEF/ACS CASE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's Takeovers Panel rejected appeals from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Leighton Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . and its majority shareholder \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hochtief AG\f28 \uc2 \f2  to block or modify a takeover bid for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hochtief\f28 \uc2 \f2  by Spain's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Actividades de Construccion y Servicios SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  . (published 2233 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SONIC HEALTHCARE\f28 \uc2 \f2  TO ACQUIRE US PATHOLOGY LAB CBLPATH FOR US$123.5M \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sonic Healthcare\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Monday it reached an agreement to acquire CBLPath, a New York-based pathology laboratories company, for US$123.5 million. (published 2246 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SK TELECOM\f28 \uc2 \f2  TO PROVIDE CONTENT FOR LENOVO'S ANDROID-BASED SMARTPHONES IN CHINA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's \f28 \uc2 \f2 SK Telecom Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday that it will supply mobile content for smartphones made by China's top personal-computer maker \f28 \uc2 \f2 Lenovo Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., in a move that would help the mobile phone carrier to strengthen its presence in the highly-competitive content distribution market. (published 0117 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CAPITAMALLS ASIA UNIT TO BUY 66% INTEREST IN SHANGHAI MALL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore-based property group \f28 \uc2 \f2 CapitaMalls Asia Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday its unit has signed a deal to purchase 66% interest in an upcoming mall and office complex in Shanghai. (published 0024 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =WSJ: AOL HIRES ADVISER TO EXPLORE STRATEGIC OPTIONS - SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 AOL Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has hired financial advisers to explore various strategic options for the company, one of which includes a possible tie-up with bigger rival \f28 \uc2 \f2 Yahoo Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., people familiar with the matter said. (published 0211 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: QANTAS SAYS OIL LEAKS FOUND IN A380 FLEET ROLLS-ROYCE ENGINES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Qantas Airways Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . on Monday said its engineers found oil leaks in Rolls-Royce Group Ltd. engines on three of its grounded fleet of A380 jetliners amid an investigation into the blowout of a turbine that forced one of its double-deck superjumbos to make an emergency landing in Singapore last week. (published 0639 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NTT\f28 \uc2 \f2  DOCOMO: TO LAUNCH HIGH-SPEED DATA NETWORK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NTT DoCoMo Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday that next month it will start offering a new data communication service using a high-speed transmission technology called long-term evolution in Japan. (published 0509 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BUMI RESOURCES MINERAL SETS INDICATIVE IPO PRICE AT IDR625-IDR635/SHARE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PT Bumi Resources\f28 \uc2 \f2  Mineral Monday set an indicative price of IDR625-IDR635 a share for its planned initial public offering slated later this year, through which it aims to sell a 22.53% stake. (published 0537 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UMC OCTOBER REVENUE RISES 15% ON YEAR TO NT$10.70 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwan's \f28 \uc2 \f2 United Microelectronics Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday its revenue in October rose 15% to NT$10.70 billion from NT$9.30 billion a year earlier. (published 0635 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ISUZU MOTORS\f28 \uc2 \f2  RETURN TO PROFITABILITY IN 1H, UPS FISCAL YEAR PROFIT OUTLOOK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Isuzu Motors Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday that it returned to profitability in the fiscal first half on solid sales in Asia and lifted its net profit outlook for the full year thanks to progress in cost-cutting. (published 0633 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES MIXED; SYDNEY DRAGGED BY QANTAS WOES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian shares were mixed Monday, with Qantas Airways denting Australia's market on concerns over the health of its fleet of Airbus A380s, while Tokyo shares climbed after better-than-expected U.S. jobs data Friday. (published 0408 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =OIL DATA: THAI SEPTEMBER CRUDE-OIL IMPORTS 793,000 B/D, -11% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's crude-oil imports in September fell 11% from a year earlier and 3.7% from August to 793,000 barrels a day, data from the Ministry of Energy showed Monday. (published 0424 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =INDIA OCTOBER STEEL OUTPUT UP 5.5% AT 5.13 MLN TONS - OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 08-11-10 0711GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's finished steel output in October rose 5.5% from a year earlier to 5.13 million metric tons on expectations of a pickup in demand after the seasonal monsoon rains, a steel ministry official said Monday. (published 0628 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par VIETNAM COFFEE STOCKPILE, OUTPUT TO LIKELY UP PRICES -OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vietnam, the world's second-largest exporter of coffee, will likely stockpile 300,000 metric tons of coffee from December onward, the chairman of Vietnam Coffee and Cocoa Association, or Vicofa, said Monday. The stockpile target, which has been approved by the government, is 50% bigger than the country's previous stockpile, made in March 2010. (published 0401 GMT) [ 08-11-10 0711GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020101108e6b8000my\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
