\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 662 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 November 2010\par 07:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOJ: JAPAN ECONOMIC RECOVERY PAUSING; PACE OF GROWTH PACE TO SLOW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan said in its monthly economic report for November that the nation's economic recovery "seems to be pausing" although there are still "signs of a moderate recovery," using a slightly weaker tone than in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's previous report in October. (published 0519 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN FINANCE MINISTER NODA: STRONG YEN HAS ADVANTAGES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance minister emphasized Monday that the strong yen has "advantages," urging domestic companies to use it buy foreign firms and assets. (published 0054 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN INTERVENED\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MARKET ONLY ONCE IN SEPTEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Official data on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  showed Friday that the authorities waded into the market only once in the July-September period, lowering expectations there could be fresh attempts to drive the yen down, even as it remains near a record high against the dollar. (published 0411 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: GEITHNER SEEKS TO BOLSTER INDIA TIES AHEAD OF G-20 SUMMIT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Seeking to bolster strategic ties with India, U.S. Treasury Secretary Timothy Geithner Monday praised the emerging economy's balanced growth and exchange-rate flexibility. (published 0134 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA MINISTER: 2010 INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT TO RISE OVER 13.5% - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's industrial output will likely rise by more than 13.5% this year, and the country's chances of meeting its full-year energy efficiency targets have increased, the China Securities Journal reported Monday, citing Minister of Industry and Information Technology Li Yizhong. (published 0059 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: S KOREA MAY TIGHTEN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  DERIVATIVES RULES PENDING PROBE OUTCOME \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean regulators may tighten existing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  derivatives regulations depending on the results of a scheduled probe into banks' activities in the market, a senior government official said Monday, as Seoul grows increasingly wary of the systemic threat posed by rapid foreign capital flows. (published 0422 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: NZ GOVERNMENT 3-MONTH OPERATING DEFICIT WIDER THAN FORECAST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The New Zealand government's core operating deficit was wider than forecast in the three months ended Sept. 30 due to the impact of the Canterbury earthquake and lower-than-forecast tax revenue, the Treasury said Monday. (published 0048 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UK CAMERON HEADS TO CHINA TARGETING DEEPER COMMERCIAL TIES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Prime Minister David Cameron will lead the U.K.'s largest-ever business delegation to China Monday, hoping to cash in on what has become a steady relationship between the two countries in recent years. (published 0001 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par GOODMAN GROUP PRICES 10-YEAR US$325M BOND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goodman Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Monday it priced a US$325 million 10-year debt issue. (published 0340 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: EXIM BANK TO OFFER UP TO CNY5 BLN BONDS IN HK AT 2.65% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Export-Import Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Monday it plans to offer up to CNY5 billion worth of yuan-denominated bonds in Hong Kong from Tuesday to Nov. 26. (published 0535 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par OCBC SEEKS TO RAISE $500 MLN VIA 12-YEAR LOWER TIER 2 ISSUE - SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Oversea-Chinese Banking Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is seeking to raise $500 million through a lower Tier-2 note issue, people familiar with the transaction said Monday. (published 0411 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par  \par =PREVIEW: JAPAN 3Q GDP GROWTH SEEN UP, BUT RISK OF RECESSION AHEAD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's economic expansion likely accelerated in the third quarter of 2010 as shoppers scrambled to buy cars before government subsidies ran out, air conditioners to stay cool in a scorching summer, and cigarettes before a new tobacco tax kicked in. (published 0425 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =PREVIEW: CHINA OCTOBER TRADE SURPLUS LIKELY REBOUNDED TO $26.4 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's trade surplus likely rebounded in October after narrowing in September, which would give critics of the country's exchange rate policy extra ammunition just as leaders of the Group of 20 industrial and developing nations gather in Seoul later this week to debate global imbalances. (published 0437 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 08-11-10 0600GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020101108e6b8000ea\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
