\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Focus: Bank Of Japan Can't Relax For Long\b0\par\par\uc2 By Nicholas Hastings   \par \uc2 A DOW JONES NEWSWIRES COLUMN   \par \uc2 745 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 November 2010\par 13:03\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--The Bank of Japan must be sighing with relief.\par \par \uc2 But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be well advised not to relax too much just yet.\par \par \uc2 Like an ambulance, the Bank of Japan raced to the sight of a possible accident this week but in the end there was no disaster.\par \par \uc2 So, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's officials wrap up their meeting in Tokyo early Friday morning, they will more than likely just tinker with their previous policy arrangements rather than announce any new drastic measures to stop the yen from rising against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Not only did the U.S. Federal Reserve produce a policy shift late Wednesday well within the market's expectations but the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's additional quantitative easing had very little impact on the dollar's performance against the yen.\par \par \uc2 The problem for the Bank of Japan, though, is the dollar is falling sharply everywhere else.\par \par \uc2 See how the dollar has stayed relatively steady against the yen:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.dowjoneswebservices.com/chart/view/4887"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.dowjoneswebservices.com/chart/view/4887}}}\par \par \uc2 See how the euro has soared against the dollar:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.dowjoneswebservices.com/chart/view/4888"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.dowjoneswebservices.com/chart/view/4888}}}\par \par \uc2 There are only two likely reasons why the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't falling against the yen as well.\par \par \uc2 One is that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market participants are so scared of another round of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that they are keeping well away from pushing the dollar back down below the key Y80 that will make exporters scream.\par \par \uc2 The other possible reason is that the Bank of Japan and its club of close banking cohorts are in the market already, buying the dollar against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a surreptitious exercise to stop the yen from rising.\par \par \uc2 However, neither of these two will influence the market for long.\par \par \uc2 The last Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  exercise in the middle of September may have been the largest ever conducted by the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But, as the dollar's continued slide against the yen since then has proved, unilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't really work.\par \par \uc2 In other words, the Bank of Japan would need the support of other major central banks, and most importantly the Fed, if \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is to succeed in turning the yen around.\par \par \uc2 History shows that the success of surreptitious \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also limited. Not only does it fail to have the big impact of large and obvious \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action, but also it requires monetary policy to be pointed in the right direction. In this case, further Bank of Japan easing would be needed to bring about a sustained fall in the yen.\par \par \uc2 So, while the dollar may be holding up against the yen for now, it will more than likely resume its slide at a later date, just when conditions in the Japanese economy are already starting to deteriorate even more.\par \par \uc2 As Prime Minister Naoto Kan warned earlier Thursday, hopes for self-sustained growth just haven't been realized.\par \par \uc2 "Unfortunately the recovery has not gone that far and downside risks for the economy are increasing," Kan said.\par \par \uc2 How long it takes the Bank of Japan to act could depend on just how far the dollar weakens elsewhere. Analysts at \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  said that Japan could prove to be more tolerant of a weak dollar, as long as its decline against other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  helps to push them down against the yen.\par \par \uc2 In other words, the weakness of the dollar would be offset by a rally in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as it would help to get Japan's export growth back on track.\par \par \uc2 Bloomberg TNI FRX POV\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Reuters   USD/DJ \par    Thomson   P/1066 or P/1074 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Nick Hastings has covered the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets and industry for over 20 years. Apart from his written commentary and analysis, he also appears on Fox Business News and CNBC television in Europe, Asia and the U.S. He can be contacted on +44-20-7842-9493 or by email: nick.hastings@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TALK BACK: We invite readers to send us comments on this or other financial news topics. Please email us at TalkBackEurope@dowjones.com. Readers should include their full names, work or home addresses and telephone numbers for verification purposes. We reserve the right to edit and publish your comments along with your name; we reserve the right not to publish reader comments. [ 04-11-10 1203GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1066   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020101104e6b40019z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
