\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 1,018 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 November 2010\par 07:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: BOJ SHIRAKAWA CALLS CURRENT RATES "MOST APPROPRIATE" \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan Gov. Masaaki Shirakawa said Thursday he thinks the levels of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's current policy target rate and interest on private banks' reserve accounts are appropriate, suggesting a reduced possibility of imminent rate cuts. (published 0540 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FINANCE MINISTER NODA: WILL \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MARKET IF NECESSARY \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister reiterated Thursday that the government can't ignore sharp rises in the yen and that it will again \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market if necessary. (published 0520 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: CHINA ADVISER: NATIONS COULD TEAM UP AGAINST DOLLAR FALL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China could team up with other countries dissatisfied with the U.S. dollar's fall to prevent excessive depreciation of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Li Deshui, vice director of the Economic Commission of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference, wrote in an essay published Thursday in the China Information News. (published 0346 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INDIA'S FISCAL GOALS THROUGH 2015 BASED ON GLOBAL CONDITIONS - OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's aim to cut its reliance on government borrowing hinges on global economic conditions and buoyant revenue flow, a senior finance ministry official said Thursday. (published 0411 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DATA SNAP: AUSTRALIA SEP TRADE SURPLUS A$1.76B \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's seasonally adjusted balance on trade in goods and services narrowed to a surplus of A$1.76 billion in September from a surplus of A$2.45 billion in August, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said Thursday. (published 0034 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: AUSTRALIAN RETAIL SALES SHOW TEPID GROWTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian retail sales showed only tepid growth during September as households continue to watch their spending despite an otherwise robust economy with near full employment. (published 0148 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: AUSTRALIAN CENTRAL BK'S CORBETT TIPS CHRISTMAS RETAIL SALES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A board member of Australia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Thursday he expects retail sales during the key Christmas shopping period to be strong, shrugging off concerns that high interest rates and the increased cost of living for homeowners are putting pressure on consumers. (published 0250 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOK: NEED TO HAVE CAPACITY FOR POLICY RESPONSE AGAINST SHOCKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Korea said Thursday that the country needs to secure capacity for policy responses against any unexpected financial shocks because of the heightened uncertainty in the global economy. (published 0300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par OFFICIAL: S KOREA TO 'ACTIVELY' SEEK MEASURES TO CURB INFLOWS AFTER US EASING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean government will "actively" seek further measures to curb excessive capital inflows after the U.S. Federal Reserve unveiled plans for further bond purchases overnight, a senior official at the Ministry of Strategy and Finance said Thursday. (published 0031 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: S KOREA GOVERNMENT SAYS TO OPERATE MACRO POLICIES IN STABLE WAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean government will implement macroeconomic policies to ensure the economy continues recovering over the long term, the Ministry of Strategy and Finance said Thursday, even as it stressed the presence of great external uncertainties. (published 0128 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =3RD UPDATE: NEW ZEALAND UNEMPLOYMENT FALLS, BUT RBNZ TO STAND PAT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's unemployment rate fell in the third quarter, sending the local dollar to its highest level in two and a half years, but the reading likely won't be enough to spur the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to raise interest rates. (published 0437 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREANS INVEST $24.79B OVERSEAS IN FIRST 9 MONTHS; UP 84.7% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Koreans invested a total of $24.79 billion overseas in the first nine months of this year, 84.7% more than in the same period last year and recovering to pre-crisis levels, the Ministry of Strategy and Finance said Thursday. (published 0559 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par PHILIPPINE TAX AGENCY: OCT COLLECTION TOPS PHP54.9 BLN YEAR-EARLIER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippines' Bureau of Internal Revenue, the government's main tax-collection agency, Thursday said preliminary tax collection for October has already exceeded revenue generated in the same period last year, but didn't say if the target for the month had been met. (published 0403 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par HKMA CHAN: FED STIMULUS PLAN RAISES RISK OF PROPERTY BUBBLE IN HK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Chief Executive Norman Chan said Thursday the U.S. Federal Reserve's latest stimulus measures will likely lead to more fund flows to markets like Hong Kong, raising the risk of a property bubble in the city. (published 0139 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S OPPOSITION TO INTRODUCE PRIVATE BILL ON BANK COMPETITION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's main conservative opposition said Thursday it will seek greater powers for the country's competition watchdog so that it can crack down on commercial banks engaging in anti-competitive behavior. (published 0102 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: INDONESIA PRICES Y60 BLN SAMURAI BONDS TO YIELD 1.6% -SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Indonesian government Thursday priced Y60 billion Samurai bonds to yield 1.6%, as solid demand for the Southeast Asian country's second yen-denominated issuance allowed it to increase the size of the deal, a banker familiar with the deal said. (published 0457 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par GOODMAN FUNDING SEEKS TO SELL $250M 10-YEAR BOND - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's Goodman Funding Pty Ltd is seeking to sell $250 million in 10-year global bonds, according to a person close to the deal Thursday. (published 0101 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PTT SETS COUPONS FOR DUAL-TRANCHE BONDS WORTH UP TO THB10 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PTT PCL\f28 \uc2 \f2  has set the coupons for its dual-tranche bond issue that is worth up to THB10 billion . (published 0404 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PETRON: LAUNCHED MAIDEN PHP20 BLN PESO GLOBAL BOND DUE 2017 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Petron Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., the Philippines' largest oil refiner by capacity and sales, Thursday said it launched overnight its maiden PHP20 billion peso-denominated global bond due November 2017. (published 0341 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par  \par =PREVIEW: TAIWAN OCTOBER CPI LIKELY UP 0.5% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Higher food prices stemming from agricultural damages due to flooding caused by Typhoon Megi likely pushed Taiwan's consumer price index higher for a second straight month in October, after the island's CPI dipped in August. (published 0442 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =HEARD ON THE STREET: CAPTAIN BEN CHARTS A TREACHEROUS COURSE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Another day, another surge into uncharted territory. (published 2326 GMT) [ 04-11-10 0600GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020101104e6b4000dp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
