\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Euro Up Vs Dollar On RBA Rate Hike; May Rise More\b0\par\par\uc2 By Takashi Mochizuki   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 592 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 November 2010\par 06:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The euro rose against the dollar in Asia on Tuesday due to knock-on effects from the Australian dollar's surge, which was propelled by the \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2 's surprise interest-rate hike.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  tightened its benchmark cash rate by 25 basis points to 4.75%, a move traders said was a big surprise. Many market participants had believed the RBA would leave rates unchanged.\par \par \uc2 "The view was widespread that the RBA won't raise its rates at least until December because recent economic data have been weak," said Jun Kato, a senior dealer at Shinkin Asset Management.\par \par \uc2 While the Australian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose sharply, the euro also benefited from the rate hike as the two \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are closely correlated.\par \par \uc2 The Australian dollar rose to $0.9990 from $0.9881 and to Y80.43 from Y79.63 before the RBA's announcement. The euro was at $1.3927 and Y112.16 as of 0450 GMT from $1.3885 and Y111.91 on Monday in New York.\par \par \uc2 Dealers in Tokyo said the dollar should keep weakening against not only the euro but also the yen, as short-term speculators are decreasing their holdings of the greenback ahead of a two-day Federal Open Market Committee meeting ending Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Many investors think the FOMC will take additional easing measures to prop up the economy. This should push down yields on U.S. bonds and make the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  less attractive.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was at Y80.52 at 0450GMT from Y80.60, and dealers said it could fall below the all-time low of Y79.75 later in the global day.\par \par \uc2 "Many investors are hungry for a chance to justify their dollar-selling even before the FOMC," said Kenichi Nishii, a senior dealer at \uc2 Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi\uc2  UFJ.\par \par \uc2 Earlier Tuesday, Japanese Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda reiterated his warning against sharp moves in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, saying the government "will take decisive steps when necessary."\par \par \uc2 But investors shrugged off the remarks because they think \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  can't take dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to possible U.S. discomfort toward such an \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The ICE Dollar Index, which tracks the greenback against a trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was at 77.090 from 77.294.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Interbank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Rates At 00:50 EDT / 0450 GMT \par  \par                          Latest     Previous   %Chg   Daily   Daily    %Chg \par Dollar Rates                        2150 GMT          High    Low      12/31 \par  \par  \par USD/JPY Yen              80.50-52   80.50-54    0.00  80.75   80.49   -13.52 \par EUR/USD Euro             1.3927-29  1.3891-92  +0.26  1.3932  1.3882   -2.72 \par GBP/USD Sterling         1.6055-59  1.6036-40  +0.12  1.6065  1.6037   -0.67 \par USD/CHF Swiss Franc      0.9906-15  0.9919-33  -0.13  0.9932  0.9907   -4.33 \par USD/CAD Canadian Dlr     1.0114-21  1.0164-70  -0.49  1.0156  1.0117   -3.80 \par AUD/USD Australian Dlr   0.9980-84  0.9866-71  +1.16  0.9991  0.9861  +11.10 \par NZD/USD New Zealand Dlr  0.7656-66  0.7667-75  -0.14  0.7673  0.7640   +5.51 