\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE:  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  MOF Says No  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\uc2  In October\b0\par\par\uc2 466 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Oktober 2010\par 14:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds further background on \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Kosaku Narioka \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  refrained from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in October, \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  figures showed Friday, with the authorities sitting on the sidelines despite the yen's continued rise to near-record levels.\par \par \uc2 The figures covered the period Sept. 29 to Oct. 27.\par \par \uc2 The inaction was in sharp contrast to the previous month when Japan surprised the market by selling Y2.125 trillion in the market to help tame the yen's persistent climb against the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , all of which is believed to have taken place on Sept. 15, succeeded in temporarily stanching the fall of the dollar, pushing the greenback from just below Y83 up to around Y85.65.\par \par \uc2 But the dollar has since then faced severe selling pressure across the board, falling as far as around Y80.50--close to the all-time low of Y79.75 reached in April 1995.\par \par \uc2 The question of why Japan has kept out of the market has been a hot topic in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 Japanese authorities have refused to divulge their plans even as Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda, whose ministry is responsible for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  issues, has repeatedly stated that Japan is watching the markets carefully and will take decisive action when necessary.\par \par \uc2 Market analysts and traders have formulated their own views, pointing to the international friction that could result if Japan decides to repeatedly enter the market to keep the dollar from falling. The meeting last weekend of the Group of 20 industrial and developing nations agreed that the member nations will "move towards more market determined exchange rate systems that reflect underlying economic fundamentals and refrain from competitive devaluation of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has countered that its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not fall into this category since it was designed to smooth out market volatility, not to alter the market's basic direction.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , conducted a day after Prime Minister Naoto Kan won a second term as head of the ruling Democratic Party of Japan, was largely tailored to a domestic audience, a person familiar with the matter told Dow Jones Newswires recently.\par \par \uc2 The move was meant to "show leadership" to voters, the person said, adding that Finance Minister Noda had long been reluctant to authorize \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But faced with intense pressure from the Prime Minister's office, particularly from Chief Cabinet Secretary Yoshito Sengoku, Noda ordered the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell the yen, the person said.\par \par \uc2 The MOF plans to release more detailed data on the September \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  around early November.\par \par \uc2 -By Kosaku Narioka, Dow Jones Newswires; 81-3-6269-2783; kosaku.narioka@dowjones.com [ 29-10-10 1202GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020101029e6at001se\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
