\par\par \b \uc2 =DJ ASIA DAILY  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  OUTLOOK: Predicted Ranges, Themes-2-\b0\par\par\uc2 953 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Oktober 2010\par 02:33\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2010, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 USD/JPY to consolidate amid broad-based USD weakness (ICE spot dollar index last 77.28 vs Wednesday''''s 78.149 settlement) as market participants await U.S. 3Q GDP data (forecast +2.1%) due 1230 GMT. Although smaller scale of U.S. Federal Reserve quantitative easing Wednesday now discounted, USD under pressure as market participants shift focus to uncertainty over whether \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will announce finite amount of easing or leave it open-ended with liquidity being provided as needed in coming months. USD/JPY also undermined by Japan exporter sales, lower U.S. Treasury yields. But USD/JPY losses tempered by USD demand for import settlements, fear of further \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  MOF JPY-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , speculation of further BOJ monetary easing after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  yesterday brought forward its next meeting to Nov. 4-5 (just after FOMC meeting) from Nov. 15-16.\par \par \uc2  Pair also could be supported by weekend as well as month-end positions adjustment; JPY-funded carry trades amid better risk sentiment as U.S. stocks recovered from early losses to close mixed (DJIA off 0.1%, S&P up 0.1%); still, (VIX fear gauge ended up 0.82% at 20.88). Other data focus: 2330 GMT Japan September Nation CPI, October Tokyo CPI, Japan September household spending, September labour force survey, 2350 GMT Japan September preliminary industrial production, 0500 GMT Japan September housing starts, September construction orders, 1230 GMT U.S. 3Q employment cost index, October ISM-NY report on business, 1245 GMT October ISM-Chicago business survey, 1355 GMT October University of Michigan survey of consumers (final). USD/JPY daily chart mixed as MACD bullish; but stochastics neutral, 5-day moving average meandering sideways below 15-day. Resistance at 81.41 (hourly chart), then at 81.77 (yesterday''''s high) and 82.00 (Oct. 13 high); breach would expose upside to 82.34 (Oct. 12 high), then 82.57 (Oct. 8 high), 82.87 (previous base set Sept. 15) and 83.02 (Oct. 7 high). Support at 80.84 (yesterday''''s low); breach would, expose downside to 80.59 (Tuesday''''s low), then 80.41 (Monday''''s 15-year low), psychological 80.00 and 79.75 (record low set April 19, 1995).\par \par \uc2 GBP/USD to consolidate as market await U.S. 3Q GDP data. Pair underpinned by surprise rise in UK GfK consumer confidence to minus 19 in October from minus 20 last month (vs forecast for drop to minus 24), negative USD sentiment, better-then expected CBI October retail sales balance of +36 (vs +30 forecast), reduced odds of more BOE bond purchases in November following Tuesday''''s better-than-forecast 3Q GDP report; higher investor risk tolerance. But GBP sentiment dented by 0.7% fall in Nationwide October UK house prices (vs forecast for 0.4% drop). GBP/USD gains also tempered by lingering concerns over negative impact of fiscal tightening on UK economy, positions adjustment ahead of week-, month-ends. Data focus: 0830 GMT UK September BSA savings & mortgage lending figures, September BOE lending to individuals figures. GBP/USD daily chart mixed as stochastics bullish, but MACD still in bearish mode. Support at 1.5880 (hourly chart), then at 1.5760 (yesterday''''s low) and 1.5728 (Wednesday''''s low); breach would target 1.5690 (Tuesday''''s low), then 1.5653 (Oct. 22 low, near 55-day moving average), 1.5603 (61.8% Fibonacci correction of advance from Sept. 7 low of 1.5294 to Oct. 15 high of 1.6104) and 1.5501 (Sept. 21 low, matching 100-day moving average). Resistance at 1.5976 (yesterday''''s high); breach would target 1.6003 (Oct. 18 high), then 1.6104 (8-month high set Oct. 15), 1.6276 (Jan. 28 high) and 1.6457 (Jan. 19 reaction high).\par \par \uc2 EUR/JPY to consolidate as market awaits U.S. 3Q GDP data. Cross supported by increased investor risk tolerance, threat of further \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  JPY-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , prospect of further BOJ monetary easing at its next meeting Nov. 4-5; Japan importer demand. But EUR/JPY gains tempered by Japan exporter sales, positions adjustment ahead of week-, month-ends. Daily chart mixed as MACD bearish, 5- & 15-day moving averages falling; but stochastics neutral. Support at 112.36 (hourly chart), then at 112.16 (yesterday's low); breach would expose downside to 111.54 (Oct. 20 low, near 100-day moving average), then 111.20 (55-day moving average), 110.63 (Sept. 16 low) and 109.55 (previous cap set Aug. 30). Resistance at 112.97 (yesterday's high), then at 113.13 (downtrend resistance line from Oct. 7 high of 115.66); breach would target 113.27 (Tuesday's high), then 113.77 (Monday's high), 113.94 (Oct. 21 high), 114.79 (Oct. 14 high) and 114.95 (Oct. 8 high).\par \par \uc2 EUR/GBP to consolidate with risks skewed lower. Cross undermined by reduced odds of more BOE bond purchases next month. Daily chart negative-biased as MACD & stochastics bearish; 5-day moving average staging bearish crossover against 15-day. Support at 0.8709 (hourly chart), then at 0.8699-0.8696 band (yesterday's low-Oct. 12 low); breach would target 0.8682 (Oct. 6 low), then 0.8635 (38.2% Fibonacci correction of 0.8139-0.8941 Aug. 23-Oct. 25 advance), 0.8624 (Oct. 5 low) and 0.8571 (200-day moving average). Resistance at 0.8752 (hourly chart), then at 0.8771 (yesterday's high); breach would expose upside to 0.8879 (Tuesday's high), then 0.8941 (Monday's 7-month high) and psychological 0.9000.\par \par \uc2 -0-\par \par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2010 \uc2 Dow Jones & Company, Inc\uc2 . \par