\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  did not conduct  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2  in Oct - MOF\b0\par\par\uc2 211 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Oktober 2010\par 12:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Oct 29 (Reuters) - Japanese authorities did not conduct any \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  between Sept. 29 and Oct. 27, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Japan stepped in to sell yen on Sept. 15 for the first time in more than six years after the dollar slid to a 15-year low against the yen, with market players estimating that Japan conducted roughly 2 trillion yen ($25 billion) in yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on that day alone.\par \par \uc2 Market players say Japanese authorities have probably stayed out of the market after that Sept. 15 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , even though the dollar has dropped further against the yen, hurt by market expectations on the U.S. Federal Reserve unveiling a second round of quantitative easing at its Nov. 2-3 policy meeting.\par \par \uc2 Traders say Japanese authorities may have a hard time justifying further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  unless the dollar's drop against the yen becomes more rapid, especially after Group of 20 economies agreed to shun \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  devaluations and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent criticism of South Korea for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (Reporting by Masayuki Kitano; Editing by Joseph Radford)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 JAPAN\b0 \highlight\uc2 -ECONOMY/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (URGENT)|LANGEN|NAT|J|SI|RBN|UKI|AUF|ND|ABN|M|E|D|U|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101029e6at001l9\par }\page {\