\par\par \b \uc2 RPT- \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar hovers above record low vs yen, Japan unhappy\b0\par\par\uc2 1,332 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Oktober 2010\par 08:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Dollar holds a yen above 1995's 79.75 yen record low\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's finance minister says \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  stance unchanged\par \par \uc2 * Dollar index little changed, euro in consolidation\par \par \uc2 By Charlotte Cooper and Masayuki Kitano\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Oct 26 (Reuters) - The dollar held just a yen above its 1995 record low against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday, prompting Japanese policy-makers to remind the market that Tokyo might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if pushed to stop its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from rising.\par \par \uc2 The dollar barely moved against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the euro failed to sustain gains the previous day back towards a recent eight-month high, highlighting the fact that the greenback is finding bouts of support.\par \par \uc2 The dollar's postwar record low of 79.75 yen set in April 1995 has become a focal point as the greenback has moved steadily lower, hitting a 15-year trough at 80.41 yen on Monday, with players wary that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if it nears 80.00 yen, following Tokyo's first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in six years in September.\par \par \uc2 But tensions among G20 partners over competitive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  devaluations have muddied the waters for Japan, which is worried yen strength is harming its fragile economy but pledged along with its G20 counterparts at the weekend to refrain from competitive devaluations. [ID:nTOE69M01E]\par \par \uc2 Still, the same pledge also said advanced economies would be vigilant against disorderly exchange rate movements, a phrase Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda was quick to point to on Tuesday while saying Japan would take decisive steps on \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  when needed. [ID:nTKF107056]\par \par \uc2 "Everyone thinks \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a possibility, that it is an option, but it is hard to say at what level that could occur," said a trader for a foreign bank in Tokyo.\par \par \uc2 The question was whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had sufficient rationale to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , given that falls in the dollar against the yen have remained gradual and not been very rapid, he said.\par \par \uc2 "It could be pretty difficult to conduct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with justification," he said.\par \par \uc2 <^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par \par \uc2 For a PDF on the G20's uneasy truce on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and trade imbalances: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/nan99p"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/nan99p}}}\par \par \uc2 For an \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  column on the Fed: [ID:nLDE69L1EY]\par \par \uc2 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^>\par \par \uc2 The dollar dipped as far as 80.66 yen <JPY=> on Tuesday before edging back to stand slightly lower on the day at 80.79.\par \par \uc2 Partly because of wariness about Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pair has hugged narrow trading bands, pushing down its one-month realised volatility to 10.2 percent, the lowest level in more than two years.\par \par \uc2 The dollar was little changed against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the dollar index <.DXY> <=USD> at 77.07. The index has support at 76.00-10 area, just below its Oct 15 low of 76.144 while resistance is seen at 78.40.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which acts on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Sept.15 for the first time since 2004 to sell the yen when it rose beyond 83.00 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 The greenback has fallen broadly since then as the market has priced in more quantitative easing by the Federal Reserve, highlighting the uphill battle \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would face if it did \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Japanese exporters needing to convert their overseas earnings are said to have sold dollars into even small dollar/yen rallies, keeping the pair under downward pressure and prompting \uc2 Nissan Motor Co\uc2 's chief operating officer to say on Tuesday he had a "huge sense of crisis" about the strong yen.[ID:nTKX007046]\par \par \uc2 Technically, chartists at \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2  said in a note that dollar/yen was in a position for a test if not a break of the 1995 low. "Still, given the short-term oversold set-up, a choppy downside bias remains likely," they said.\par \par \uc2 The euro eased 0.1 percent to $1.3947 <EUR=> after once again failing to hold above $1.4000 on Monday and keeping intact a familiar range roughly between $1.3700 and $1.4160 this month.\par \par \uc2 "It's tried a few times and failed. People are quick to lock in profit these days," said Grant Turley, a strategist at ANZ in Sydney.\par \par \uc2 The euro has support at around 1.3860, its low last Friday and its 21-day moving average at $1.3866, though a break of which could trigger a bigger correction.\par \par \uc2 With the Fed expected to pump more money into the economy as early as next week but with no clear consensus still on how much cash it will inject, analysts expect dollar pairs to stay choppy.\par \par \uc2 Keeping the market guessing, New York Fed President William Dudley said whether an incremental or big bang approach to asset purchases would work better depended on the economic context. [ID:nNLLPLE6LF]\par \par \uc2 "The market's getting mixed signals from the Fed but ultimately whatever they do they are going to be doing QE2," said a senior trader at a European bank in Hong Kong.\par \par \uc2 The market had pared its expectations of massive purchases to a more start-and-see-how-it-goes approach, he said, but in the end QE was likely to continue until unemployment began to fall.\par \par \uc2 Macro funds had trimmed some of their short dollar positions as they waited to see how the G20 \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debate shaped up, with a question mark after the weekend statement as to whether major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the euro should adjust upwards as much against the dollar as Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "That's a bit harder to gauge and if dollar/Asia starts moving lower there's still going to be some \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and there's still going to be some of that recycled into the euro and the Aussie," the senior trader said.\par \par \uc2 The Australian dollar <AUD=D4> slipped 0.1 percent to $0.9900, still unable to make a sustained push through parity.\par \par \uc2 But it was seen supported by demand stemming from corporate merger activities and heightened expectations of a near-term interest rate hike, with markets awaiting consumer inflation on Wednesday to see if the \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2  will tighten.\par \par \uc2 Markets are pricing in a 52 percent chance of a 25 basis point rate hike to the 4.5 percent benchmark rate at the Nov. 2 meeting <CSRBA=CSAU>.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Ian Chua in Sydney and Hideyuki Sano; Editing by Joseph adford) ((Email: charlotte.cooper@thomsonreuters.com; +81 3 6441 1870; Reuters Messaging: charlotte.cooper.reuters.com@reuters.net))\par \par \uc2 All data taken from Reuters calculated from the levels at 2130 GMT in the previous New York session.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                      Last  US Close    Pct   YTD Pct   2009\par                                     Change  Change    Close\par --------------------------------------------------------------\par Euro/dlr   <EUR=>      1.3975   1.3963   +0.09   -2.38   1.4316\par Dlr/yen    <JPY=>      80.660   80.780   -0.15  -13.18   92.900\par Euro/yen   <EURJPY=R>  112.73   112.81   -0.07  -15.29   133.08\par Dlr/swiss  <CHF=>      0.9706   0.9707   -0.01   -6.27   1.0355\par Stg/dlr    <GBP=>      1.5744   1.5731   +0.08   -2.54   1.6154\par Dlr/cad    <CAD=>      1.0184   1.0190   -0.06   -3.18   1.0518\par Aus/dlr    <AUD=>      0.9921   0.9912   +0.09  +10.58   0.8972\par Nzd/dlr    <NZD=>      0.7538   0.7515   +0.31   +4.07   0.7243\par Aus/yen    <AUDJPY=R>  80.010   80.050   -0.05   -4.05   83.390\par Nzd/yen    <NZDJPY=R>  60.760   60.710   +0.08   -9.70   67.290\par Stg/yen    <GBPJPY=R>  127.00   127.08   -0.06  -15.38   150.09\par Aus/Nzd    <AUDNZD=R>  1.3151   1.3169   -0.14   +6.34   1.2367\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 All spots <\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 =>\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tokyo spots <AFX=>\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Europe spots <EFX=>\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Volatilities <FXVOL=>\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market info from BOJ <TKYFX>\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 World \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news [CEN]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Economic Forecasts...<ECON>\par  Official rates...[INT/RATE]\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Diary.......[MI/DIARY]\par  Top events........[M/DIARY]\pa