\par\par \b \uc2 Q+A-Will  \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervene \highlight\uc2  again on  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2 ?\b0\par\par\uc2 1,140 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Oktober 2010\par 08:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Oct 26 (Reuters) - The dollar has fallen within spitting distance of its postwar record low against the yen and market players say Japanese authorities may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again if it falls sharply, after they did so in September.\par \par \uc2  A G20 pledge to avoid competitive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  devaluations has muddied the waters for Tokyo but policy-makers have since repeated said they will take decisive steps in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market when needed and that their stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unchanged.\par \par \uc2  But there is a growing impression among some traders that with a debate globally about competitive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  devaluation and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent criticism of South Korea for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Tokyo may not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again, even though it says it might.\par \par \uc2  The dollar has lost about 4 percent against the yen since the end of August and 13 percent so far this year, despite 2.1 trillion yen or $25 billion worth of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month, with the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold across the board after the Federal Reserve signalled it was ready to ease policy again.\par \par \uc2  The dollar dipped to its lowest in 15 years this week, to 80.41 yen <JPY=>. The market is jittery about the possibility that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  grinds down towards its 1995 postwar low of 79.75 yen.\par \par \uc2  <^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Q+A on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  capacity        [ID:nTOE68S07S]\par  Q+A on unsterilised \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2             [ID:nTOE68G02P]\par  Graphic on trade weighted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 fx\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 :   \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/qun86p"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/qun86p}}}\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  tensions map:          \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/jec96p"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/jec96p}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  For a PDF on the G20's uneasy truce on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par  and trade imbalances:           \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/nan99p"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/nan99p}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^>\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  Here are some questions and answers about \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's possible\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 :\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  WHAT MIGHT PROMPT \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  AGAIN?\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  acts on behalf of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , and those who think it might step in say\par it could do so if there was a rapid rise in the yen specifically,\par rather than a general drop in the dollar, and it was accompanied\par by a sharp drop in the Nikkei <.N225> share average.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  If yen crosses such as the euro/yen and Australian dollar/yen\par rates remain stable \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is seen as less likely. But\par general yen strength could change the equation, especially if it\par is being driven by a buildup of speculative positions.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  One catalyst could be a fall in the dollar below the record\par low, which could draw more cries of pain from exporters.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  Some traders say a sharp fall in Japanese share prices could\par also alarm the authorities and prompt \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . If the Nikkei\par falls below a 16-month low near 8,800 hit in early September, the\par Japanese government may feel more pressed to act.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  WON'T THE G20 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  WARS DEBATE STOP THEM?\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  The debate makes \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  more difficult, at a time when\par China is under pressure to allow more rapid appreciation of the\par yuan.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  G20 finance ministers agreed at the weekend to shun\par competitive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  devaluations and some players think this has\par made \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  even harder for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . [ID:nTOE69M01E]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  Tokyo has escaped overt criticism from Washington for its\par Sept. 15 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the only confirmed bout so far. But euro\par group Chairman Jean-Claude Juncker was openly critical and a G7\par source said Japan got heavy criticism from the Europeans behind\par the scenes at a G7 meeting in early October, making it very\par difficult for Tokyo to justify \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  again.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  To be sure, Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda repeated even\par after the G20 meeting that Japan will take decisive action if\par warranted. [ID:nTOE69O09F]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  And some traders suspect that Japan could point to a section\par of the G20 communique calling for vigilance against disorderly\par moves in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to justify \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  But many traders feel that the tone of Japanese\par policy-makers' comments changed after the October IMF and G7\par meetings in Washington. Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda was at\par pains to stress that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was aimed at stopping excessive\par moves from hurting the economy, rather than the start of a big,\par long campaign aimed at targeting a specific \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par level.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  Noda then criticised South Korea for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to keep down\par its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , saying Seoul's leadership of the G20 would come\par under question due to its regular \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , a barb some\par analysts took to mean: "If we can't do it, then neither can you."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  Criticising South Korea made Noda sound less likely to be\par considering immediate \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  SO WHAT IS THE AUTHORITIES' STRATEGY?\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  That's hard to fathom because of the politics involved and\par because the only confirmed \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the past six years is\par the Sept. 15 action, so the market does not have a lot to go on.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  Levels the market thought might be "lines drawn in the sand"\par have been and gone, with the next potential one at 80 yen.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  While at first some thought Sept. 15 marked the start of a\par longer campaign, now it may be that the authorities will keep the\par action confined to a few occasions when the opportunity presents\par itself to counter rapid yen moves and remind the market of the\par two-way risk.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  In the meantime, policy-makers are keeping up a steady stream\par of verbal reminders that they will act decisively when needed.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  HOW FAR IS THE YEN LIKELY TO RISE?\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  If no \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  occurs and the yen strengthens through 80\par per dollar and then 79.75, some see it moving up to 78-76 yen per\par dollar to start with. Daisuke Uno, chief strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sumitomo\par Mitsui Banking Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 , told Reuters in September that his personal\par forecast was for the yen to reach 50 next year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  A Reuters poll in early October showed a median forecast of\par 88 yen per dollar in six months' time and 92 yen in a year.\par <FXJPY>\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  A fall in the dollar below 80 yen would likely turn that\par level into resistance which the greenback could struggle to\par break.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  In the options market, implied volatilities are subdued,\par suggesting option market players expect the yen's rise to be\par slow, with one-month volatility around 11.7 percent.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  The yen's advance is likely to be slowed by various option\par barriers, which are said to be lined up at 79-80 yen.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  But a trader at a Japanese bank also noted buying in\par longer-dated dollar puts/yen calls, such as six months and nine\par months, with strike prices far below the record low of 79.75 yen,\par suggesting expectations of a deeper fall in the dollar.\par  (Reporting by Masayuki Kitano, Hideyuki Sano, Leika Kihara and\par Charlotte Cooper; Editing by Edmund Klamann and Michael Watson)\par \par \par \par \par \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Q+A)|LANGEN|J|Z|NAT|SI|UKI|AUF|ND|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101026e6aq000hm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
