\par\par \b \uc2 INSTANT VIEW 5-Japan Sept exports rise 14.4 pct year/year\b0\par\par\uc2 883 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Oktober 2010\par 03:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (For more stories on the Japanese economy click [ID:nECONJP])\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Oct 25 (Reuters) - Japan's exports rose 14.4 percent in September from a year earlier, \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed on Monday, marking the seventh straight month of slower growth as a strong yen and moderating overseas demand hurt export growth. [JPEXPY=ECI] *************************************************************\par \par \uc2 KEY POINTS:\par \par \uc2 -- Exports rose 14.4 percent in September from a year earlier, more than than economists' median forecast for a 9.6 percent rise, and imports were up 9.9 percent against an expected rise of 7.4 percent rise. [JPEXPY=ECI][JPIMPY=ECI]\par \par \uc2 -- Exports to Asia, which account for more than half of Japan's total exports, rose 14.3 percent from a year earlier.\par \par \uc2 -- Shipments to China rose 10.3 percent from a year earlier.\par \par \uc2 -- The trade balance came to a surplus 797.0 billion yen ($9.80 billion), up 54.0 percent from a year earlier. That compared with the median estimate for a 714.0 billion yen surplus and a 37.9 percent annual rise. [JPTBAL=ECI]\par \par \uc2 COMMENTARY:\par \par \uc2 SATORU OGASAWARA, ECONOMIST, CREDIT SUISSE, TOKYO\par \par \uc2 "(The BOJ) said when they decided on additional easing they saw a downside risk to the global economy and also to domestic demand. So I don't think they will change their views based on today's data since basically it is in line with expectations."\par \par \uc2 SUSUMU KATO, CHIEF ECONOMIST, CREDIT AGRICOLE\par \par \uc2 "The issue is that the yen is becoming strong against Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . So if it affects exports to Asia, Japan's exports overall may slow further.\par \par \uc2 "Also, friction with China, which could affect trade between the two nations, will be a concern as Japan depends heavily on exports to Asia.\par \par \uc2 "Amid increasing uncertainty over the economic outlook in the U.S. and Europe, the Bank of Japan will likely make downward revisions to Japan's growth and CPI (outlook) this week. The economy has not yet reached a situation where we have a clear picture that Japan will escape from deflation."\par \par \uc2 YOSHIKIYO SHIMAMINE, CHIEF ECONOMIST, DAI-ICHI LIFE RESEARCH INSTITUTE\par \par \uc2 "The numbers came in better than expected. But I see no need to change the view that exports are on a gradual slowing trend given the relative volatility of the trade data. Because of the firmer yen and the fading effects of economic stimulus in the United States, the operating environment for Japan's exports seems to be getting worse.\par \par \uc2 "Exports are up in volume terms to the U.S., Europe and Asia. But if you take a look at prices, they are down across the board, underlining exporters' efforts to drive sales by cutting prices. The corporate sector's plight from a rising yen seems to be more serious than the initial impression from the data."\par \par \uc2 YOSHIMASA MARUYAMA, ECONOMIST, \uc2 ITOCHU CORP\par \par \uc2 "The data showed that the pace of the slowdown in Japan's exports was not as bad as people had feared and it was only a mild slowdown.\par \par \uc2 "Japan's exports will likely hit bottom during October-December and January-March, and they are expected to pick up along with the global economic recovery, helped especially by demand from Asia.\par \par \uc2 "The Bank of Japan has already factored in a slowdown in the nation's exports. The global economic slowdown and a strong yen have indeed had a negative impact on the economy but the data supports the view that the recovery trend has not disappeared."\par \par \uc2 MARKET REACTION:\par \par \uc2 -- For yen updates click <FXNEWS>; for prices click <JPY=>\par \par \uc2 -- For JGB updates click <MMNEWS>, for prices click <2JGBv1>\par \par \uc2 -- For stocks click [.T], for Nikkei average click <.N225>\par \par \uc2 LINKS\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Export growth              \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/new89p"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/new89p}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  Exports by destination     \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/hew89p"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/hew89p}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  Interactive G20 graphic:   \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/men39p"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/men39p}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  PDF report on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 :     \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/gez77p"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/gez77p}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  More stories on Japan's economy              [ID:nECONJP]\par  Tables   \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.customs.go.jp/toukei/info/index_e.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.customs.go.jp/toukei/info/index_e.htm}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 BACKGROUND:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- Finance officials at a weekend Group of 20 meeting vowed to avoid competitive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  devaluations but stopped short of setting targets to reduce trade imbalances that are clouding global growth prospects. [ID:nTOE69M004]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold 2.1249 trillion yen (\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last month, according to the finance ministry. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's first \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in six years has failed to reverse the yen's rising trend. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  data for this month are due on Oct. 29.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- The Bank of Japan on Oct. 28 will likely announce an outline of its asset buying scheme it pledged to create as part of its comprehensive monetary easing decided earlier this month.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is also likely to revise down its economic forecasts and predict a very slow exit from deflation in a twice-yearly outlook report, in a sign it will keep interest rates virtually zero for several years to come.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- Japan's government last week downgraded its view on the economy for the first time since February 2009, saying it is at a standstill as the rising yen and slowing exports could derail the economic recovery. [ID:nTWKJLE640] (Reporting by Stanley White)\f28 \par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/ (INSTANT VIEW 5)|LANGEN|J|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|Z|U|C|GRO|MTL|SOF|O|OIL|NAT|UKI   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101025e6ap0001a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
