000, Ocean Group (OGC.VH) ends down 4.1% at VND25,700, \uc2 Sacombank\uc2  (STB.VH) ends +0.6% at VND15,600. Tips more gains tomorrow with key index to move in 445-450 range. (phammuoi.nguyen@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0441 GMT [Dow Jones] STI reverses gains, down 0.5% at 3162.23 midday, off 3193.84 high, after China's economic data spur some investors to cash out; "the Chinese data show slower growth coupled with higher inflation, so it's got the market a bit nervy," says dealer at local brokerage, but adds intraday correction quite healthy after STI's recent gains. UOB KayHian reiterates cautious stance "as we believe that a short-term consolidation is in play." Advises investors buy on dips before index resumes upward trend; tips 3,042 support. \uc2 Mapletree Logistics Trust\uc2  (M44U.SG) +3.4% at S$0.915 with spike in volume; trader cites talk of possible mistaken identity with \uc2 Mapletree Industrial Trust\uc2  (ME8U.SG) due to start trade after break. \uc2 Keppel Land\uc2  (K17.SG) off 0.7% at S$4.47 after reporting fall in 3Q net profit; \uc2 CapitaCommercial Trust\uc2  (C61U.SG) +0.7% at S$1.45. Decliners now outnumber gainers about 1.4 to one; 1.19 billion shares traded worth S$1.24 billion. (matthew.allen@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0437 GMT [Dow Jones] Nikkei down 0.1% at 9370.32, falling back into negative territory after posting 0.2% gain in morning session. Investors remain nervous about stronger yen trend (USD/JPY now 81.14 vs intraday high of 81.84) and amid absence of positive surprise from slew of key economic data from China (3Q GDP +9.6% vs economists' expectations of +9.5%). "With the United States expected to continue monetary easing measures for some time, it's unlikely the weaker dollar trend will change in the next 6 months to a year," says Yoshinori Nagano, senior strategist at \uc2 Daiwa Asset Management\uc2 , though noting possibility of short-term technical rebound in USD/JPY. Puts near-term support lines for Nikkei at 9360 and 9200. 24/33 Topix subindexes lower; \uc2 Central Japan Railway\uc2  (9022.TO), or "JR Central", down 6.2% at Y606,000 on concerns over funds needed to build magnetic levitation train line connecting Tokyo and Nagoya. Select exporters off; \uc2 Ricoh\uc2  (7752.TO) down 1.9% at Y1,196 and Canon (7751.TO) down 0.8% at Y3,730. \uc2 Oji Paper\uc2  (3861.TO) up 0.8% at Y372 on Nikkei report of solid outlook for April-September earnings.(kana.inagaki@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0432 GMT [Dow Jones] MOF sells Y999.8 billion of 1.8% 20-year bonds with lowest price of 100.40, yielding 1.772%; results tad stronger than market expectations. While bid-to-cover ratio deteriorates to 4.41 from 4.56 last tender, lowest tender price of 100.40 above expected 100.30, while tail much shorter at 0.04 vs 0.20. Auction results positive for now, but concerns remain about possible selling in mid-, long- tenors going forward as brokers usually need time to resell long-term JGBs auctioned, says \uc2 Shinsei Bank\uc2  deputy general manager Tomohiko Katsu. Lead JGB futures last off 0.10 at 143.54. (kazuhiro.shimamura@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0426 GMT [Dow Jones] U.S. Treasury Secretary Geithner's comment in WSJ article that major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  "roughly in alignment now" makes it harder for \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to conduct another round of JPY-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , says Masanobu Ishikawa, general manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  spot at Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  & Ueda Harlow. Ishikawa says remark presents obstacle to any more Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after Tokyo's estimated Y2 trillion JPY-selling step last month, as suggests JPY level not really high, contrary to Japan's view that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains strong. "When an official like Mr. Geithner says something like this, Japan loses its footing," Ishikawa says. "This is like saying he doesn't accept Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." Says amid broader USD weakness, USD/JPY may fall to 80.80 by end of global day vs last 81.14. Says pair may decline toward all-time low of 79.75 in coming sessions. (kosaku.narioka@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0417 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/KRW flattish at 1,127.0 vs 1,126.9 late yesterday in Seoul after wiping out earlier fall to 1,120.0 low on short covering, corporate demand amid on-going market jitters over whether local authorities might take measures to curb KRW's recent steep gains, traders say. "I think it's going to be a 1,120-1,130 range," for a while now, says local bank trader. "It's very tiring. Government officials are talking everywhere, echoing talks that more restrictions will be implemented soon...we don't know which comments we should pay attention to," says foreign bank trader. Government denies local report that it would announce further measures in early December aimed at curbing speculative foreign capital flows. (min-jeong.lee@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0417 GMT [Dow Jones] Sensex +0.6% at 19,97.50 in early trade, helped by overnight gains in U.S. markets (DJIA ended +1.2%), short-covering in some bluechips. Market breadth positive with 26 of 30 index issues higher; TCS (532540.BY) +1.5% at INR977.50 before 2Q results later today. "The start is on expected lines. With the index - down over 800 points in previous 5 sessions some buying is happening in select heavyweights," says local dealer. Adds, short-covering helping metal plays. Tips resistance at 20,080, support at 19,850. \uc2 Tata Steel\uc2  (500470.BY) +1.4% at INR624.25, \uc2 Tata Motors\uc2  (500570.BY) +1.4% at INR1,172. \uc2 Reliance Industries\uc2  (500325.BY) +1.2% at INR1,061.50, Sterlite (500900.BY) +1.2% at INR172.30. (gurdev.singh@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0408 GMT [Dow Jones] NZD/USD weaker following U.S. Treasury Secretary Geithner's comment in WSJ interview, China data; pair likely to consolidate in 0.7400-0.7535 range ahead of G-20 this weekend, says \uc2 HIFX\uc2  director of trading Mike Hollows; "The market got unsettled when Geithner made some comments about the value of the U.S. dollar against the euro, the yen and other." Geithner told WSJ that he believes major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are "roughly in alignment now." Says China data did not have much impact "as it was there or there about" expectations. Adds, little top tier data due out overnight, market will be keeping eye on protests in Europe about austerity measure but main focus now on G-20 meeting. Pair last at 0.7510 vs 0.7544 early this morning. Tips support at 0.7490 with resistance at 0.7535. (lucy.craymer@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0406 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/CNY extends losses midday, tracking weaker USD vs Asians. Pair last at 6.6482 vs 6.6514 earlier, 6.6519 last close; 6.6450-6.6500 band tipped for rest of session. "Stronger yuan demand at the end of the month should support the dollar-yuan pair next week," says Shanghai-based US bank trader; exporters routinely sell USD at month's end to banks on request of China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Adds 3Q GDP, CPI roughly within expectations, having little impact on market. (jean.yung@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0404 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/INR lower, tracking overnight USD slip, but finding support from importers, says trader with private bank; pair at 44.31 vs 44.35 late Wednesday. Adds, firm local stocks may weigh more, but downward pressure may be offset by importers looking to cover USD needs for import payments before expected repatriation of IPO-directed flows boost pair from current levels. Tips, 44.20-44.25 zone to provide firm support, but notes some long USD positions still need cover, making test of 44.20 likely within session. (bijou.george@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0359 GMT [Dow Jones] India government bonds open lower, but may find support as traders may have overreacted in rush to dump benchmark note on view it may drift into illiquidity if new 10-year note sold in January, says trader with primary dealership; 7.80% 2020 government bond at 97.70 vs 97.75 last close. "Even if you add in a pretty heavy illiquidity premium to the yield, there's still an argument for buying the current benchmark at these levels," says trader. Notes, 10-year, 12-year spreads now inverted, indicating market already more than pricing in illiquidity in 10-year note. Directionally though, market also likely to watch weekly primary price data (due later in session) very carefully for signs that inflation may remain far from ebbing, fresh uptick may stoke talk of further RBI rate hikes beginning from next policy meeting on November 2. (bijou.george@dowjones.com) [ 10-21-10 0043ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020101021e6al0003b\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (japan near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\b